    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1128">

                <pb facs="1109" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/21460</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Collector Cobb to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-14T11:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Polk. My November 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1128-f1"/> Deputy
                    Collector Customs Presidio just telegraphs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Villa forces estimated one thousand attacked Ojinaga daylight. Fighting
                            is desultory. Few Carrancistas wounded have crossed to Presidio.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
